cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use MATE in your research, please cite this software using the metadata
  below and record the version or commit used for your analysis.
type: software
title: "MATE: Multi-omics Analysis through Trajectory Embeddings"
version: "3.0.0"
authors:
- given-names: "Kumar Saurabh"
  family-names: "Singh"
- given-names: "Kawtar"
  family-names: "Ait abdelouahd"
- given-names: "Wim"
  family-names: "Vriezen"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kumarsaurabh20/MATE"
url: "https://github.com/kumarsaurabh20/MATE"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  MATE represents independently defined transcriptomics and metabolomics modules
  as fingerprints and temporal trajectories, then integrates them through joint
  embeddings and lag-aware comparisons. It supports matched-reference responses,
  reference-free ordered trajectories, and optional continuous curve fitting.
keywords:
  - multi-omics
  - transcriptomics
  - metabolomics
  - temporal trajectories
  - lag analysis
